uch a result you need to  be able to monitor your work and your  own evolution as a writer  identifying points of friction and areas  that are open to improvement  allows you to evolve your writing style  in unprecedented ways  think of writing as any skill that can  be learned and improved  through competence emerges when one is  capable of becoming aware of one's  control  over the skill continuous immersion  offers a level of understanding of the  constituents of the skill  that an untrained eye will never be able  to see  you become the writing and the writing  becomes you  a critical tipping point in my writing  career occurred when i realized that i'm  the amalgamation of my biggest  influencers the writers that inspire me  have such a strong impact on the way i  perceive words  and various writing styles that they  inevitably shape the writer that i am  today  it all started with the fundamentals of  personal growth  books like the four-hour work week by  tim ferriss  how to win friends and influence people  by dale carnegie  mastery by robert greene the power of  now by cartoli  these books really pave the path to what  would later become a more  refined version of myself as a writer  the writing of these authors  wasn't that simple but it wasn't that  complicated either  they constitute the perfect starting  point for every person who is new to  self-development  and can help every young writer  understand how proper writing works  later on i felt that i could stretch my  intellectual limits and dive into the  works of people like  sam harris jordan peterson daniel  goldman  and peter joseph to name but a few these  people examine more  challenging ideas thus the writing  illuminates a level of  intellectual depth very few people in  this world have managed to reach  when one invests the time and effort to  properly construe these ideas  one also increases the probability of  forming similar ones  eventually i started to adopt more  abstract thinking patterns and i decided  to challenge myself with  what i like to call as the pinnacle of  higher thought  this is composed of works produced by  the greatest thinkers and philosophers  across space and time people like  friedrich nietzsche  emmanuel kant arthur schopenhauer carl  jung  sigmund freud and so many others who  devoted their lives to analyzing the  human condition and  making sense of the world around us they  did so in such a potent way that one can  suggest that they  transcended the limits of ordinary  thought when you quote unquote  befriend these figures and make them  your source of inspiration  you can't help but understand that there  is so much more to writing than  mere thought articulation take for  instance this powerful passage from  niches beyond good and evil  it is the business of the very few to be  independent it is a privilege of the  strong  and whoever attempts it even with the  best right but  without being obliged to do so proves  that he is probably not only strong  but also daring beyond measure he enters  into a labyrinth  he multiplies a thousand-fold the  dangers which life  in itself already brings with it not the  list of which is that  no one can see how and where he loses  his way  becomes isolated and stored in piecemeal  by some minotaur of conscience supposing  such a one comes to grief  it is so far from the comprehension of  men that they  neither feel it nor sympathize with it  and he cannot any longer go back  he cannot even go back again to the  sympathy of man  there's so much madness in his writing  but there is also so much truth  in his madness  your language is your main tool for  articulating thought  for instance by adopting a plain english  way of speaking and writing  although you might sound more clear and  concise you're also limiting your  potential for  more elaborate thought articulation life  remains in a stagnant state and  every opportunity to raise your  intellectual standards and  understand reality be